      "data": {
        "label": "Portals: an edge that skips what is in its way"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "text",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -190
      },
      "size": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 70
      },
      "style": {
        "fontSize": 12,
        "textAlign": "center"
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Two edges run across two others. Each has a portal: the edge stops at one mark and carries on at the other, and the same number is at both ends. Click a mark to go to the other end, drag it to move it, hover it to see the whole edge. The first number is made from the order in the file; the second was typed. Choose the mark you read most easily in Preferences (Portal mark)."
      }
    },
